---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About this project">
  <main id="main">
    <div class="page-intro"><h1>A place to explore. A reason to connect.</h1><p>A community website prototype for Macon–Bibb.</p></div>
    <div class="prose"><h2>Two ways into the community</h2><p><a href="/maps/">Explore maps</a> to browse places, combine layers and see a different view of the area. Visit the <a href="/calendar/">community calendar</a> to browse dates, filter events and download a calendar file.</p>
    <h2>Everything here is a preview</h2><p>The event listings are fictional demonstration content. No gathering shown here has been scheduled through this project. The voting map uses uploaded polling-place and precinct data, including historical and unclassified records. Other community map layers are illustrative. The home page’s map is an AI-generated illustration, not a geographic reference.</p><p>This prototype does not claim affiliation with Macon–Bibb County or any organization mentioned in the sample content. Use verified sources for event schedules, services and navigation.</p>
    <h2>Built to stay simple</h2><p>This is a static Astro website prepared for Cloudflare Pages. Event content and geographic layers can be updated as files and published with the next build. There is no account, event submission form or required application server.</p>
    <h2>Explore your way</h2><p>The map’s place directory offers the same features as the selected geographic layers. Use it to find a place and show it on the map. The calendar provides both month and agenda views, and event downloads include an explicit sample label.</p><p><a href="/data/">See the datasets and sources</a>.</p></div>
  </main>
</Layout>
